{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to write drafts as uncommitted, unstaged edits to the book with no draft marker, adding a new chapter file to `SUMMARY.md` and recording it with `git add -N`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has one obligation: the `habeas-requirements` skill must direct agents to (a) write drafts as uncommitted, unstaged edits, (b) use no draft marker, and (c) for a new chapter, add it to `SUMMARY.md` and record it with `git add -N`.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_writes_drafts_as_unstaged_edits_without_markers]` covers all of these. It finds the workflow step containing \"Write drafts\" in the bundled `habeas-requirements` skill, using `step_of` and `step`. Both go through `workflow_steps`, which parses the skill's \"Workflow\" section. `assert_text` then checks that the step contains two phrases:\n- \"Write drafts from the request straight into the chapter as uncommitted, unstaged edits, with no draft marker\" covers (a) and (b).\n- \"For a new chapter, add it to `SUMMARY.md` and `git add -N` it\" covers (c).\n\n`assert_text` asserts `contains` for each phrase, so the assertions fail if the skill text drops any of them. The requirement is about what the skill text directs, so checking that text is the right level of test. No other conditions, modes or boundary cases are named.",
